 36CA    9BE(37CA,XG):XUNDL-1          2007DO11                           200705
 36CA c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2007Do11:                          
 36CA2c  Phys Lett B 647, 237 (2007)                                            
 36CA c  Compiled by: S. Geraedts, J. Roediger and B. Singh (McMaster),         
 36CA2c  Apr 25, 2007                                                           
 36CA c  Identification of the first excited state in {+36}Ca.                  
 36CA c  {+36}Ca ions were produced via two-step fragmentation technique,       
 36CA2c  using the FRS-RISING setup at GSI. Primary {+40}Ca beam at             
 36CA3c  420 MeV/nucleon impinged a {+9}Be target. The {+37}Ca fragments were   
 36CA4c  selected on the basis of energy loss, magnetic rigidity and            
 36CA5c  time-of-flight. The {+37}Ca ions at an energy of 196 MeV/nucleon hit   
 36CA6c  a second {+9}Be target. The reaction products were selected using      
 36CA7c  calorimeter telescope array (CATE) of Si-CsI(Tl) modular               
 36CA8c  |DE-E telescopes.                                                      
 36CA c  Measured E|g, particle-|g coin, using 15 Cluster Ge detectors          
 36CA2c  with seven elements in each cluster, seven six-fold MINIBALL triple Ge 
 36CA3c  detectors, and the HECTOR array of eight large-volume BAF{-2}          
 36CA4c  detectors. Fragment trajectories were determined using the the CATE    
 36CA5c  array, and a thin Si|dE detector. The |g-ray spectra were              
 36CA6c  Doppler-corrected using Monte Carlo simulation GEANT4, corrected for   
 36CA7c  fragmentation of the primary beam using time-of-flight information.    
 36CA  L 0            0+                102 MS   2                              
 36CA cL T$ from 'adopted levels' dataset for {+36}Ca in ENSDF                  
 36CA  L 3015      16 2+                                                        
 36CA cL J$ from systematics and shell model calculations.                      
 36CA cL E$ mirror energy difference |DE{-M}=E({+36}Ca)-E({+36}S)=-276 {I16}    
 36CA2cL for the first excited 2+ states in {+36}Ca and {+36}S. The energy      
 36CA3cL of the 2+ excited state in {+36}S is at 3291 keV from literature.      
 36CA4cL 2007Do11 interpret this large |DE{-M} value in terms of detailed       
 36CA5cL shell-model calculations using {+16}O core, the {Isd} shell isospin    
 36CA6cL symmetric interaction, and experimental single particle energies       
 36CA7cL from {+17}O and {+17}F.                                                
 36CA  G 3015      16                                                           
 36CA cG E$ statistical unertainty of 15 keV and systematic uncertainty         
 36CA2cG (from energy calibration) of 5 keV, added in quadrature.               
 36CA3cG An independent experiment at GANIL facility has also detected          
 36CA4cG a |g transition at 3025 {I30} (2006BuZW: AIP Conf. Proc. 831 (2006))   
                                                                                
